Z||000004||BlackARROW||10-01-2001||03:17 AM||||Mine doesn't work either - but used too.<P>Anyway, I would have smashed it to stop annoying me, trying to influence my judgement when to shift or not  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> hehe..<P><P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"||||reg||1
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||10-01-2001||06:39 AM||||The Upshift light in the V6 cars is not connected to anything (as far as I can tell, and at least in the 1988 models...).<P>When I got my Formula, it was in excellent shape, very well cared for. One of the turn signal lamps in the instrument pod had burned out, so I disassembled it to replace that bulb and to redo the fluorescent coloring inside the panel to make it brighter/more red. <P>When I opened it up, there was no bulb in the spot for the Upshift light. I swapped bulbs around from the existing, working bulbs, and added the two brand-new bulbs into the mix, but no matter what bulb I had in the Upshift light slot (taking to for a drive around the block after switching things around) that I am sure if it was hooked up to anything, it would have come on during any one of the half-dozen trial runs I took that morning. <P>My theory is that since the 4-cyl was made for "Economy" driving, they put the Upshift light in there, but by the time they started putting the V6's in there, they figured if the buyer is getting a V6, they're more interested in performance than economy, and would be more apt to not like being told how to drive anyway. <P>My direct experience is '88-only, so I can't speak for previous years.<P><BR>EDIT - oh, mine's a 5-speed, too. Not an automatic.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||10-01-2001||07:49 AM||||My 87GT 5 speed and 86SE 4 speed both have working shift lights. The signal is taken from intake vacume and indicates economy shift point. It doesn't mean shift or your engine will blow. mine was on a good portion of the RFTH,s. I don't know about the 88's.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||10-01-2001||08:13 AM||||The upshift light never worked since day one on my 87 GT five speed (like the car had 5 miles on the odometer when I bought it). I'll have to check it out sometime when I take the front dash panel off to replace a burned out bulb in my tach.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||10-01-2001||08:49 AM||||The upshift light doesn't work in my Formula, either.  I don't think the V6's used one.||||reg||13
Z||000009||Rodrv6||10-01-2001||09:10 AM||||The owners manual for my 88 says that the upshift light is only for the L-4 engine with manual transmission.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
