Z||000012||SLYGUY||10-01-2001||02:59 PM||||Thanks for the info.<P>My 88GT is a 5spd, and my 86 SEV6 was a 4spd.<P>The theory behind it is sound. The fiero was intended to *gulp* be a "commuter" car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  and was designed by the brass at GM to meet their CAFE fuel standards ahead of time when it was introduced.<P>I liked the 4 banger okay. Like the V6 much better. Makes sense that they would like to see you get the best MPG out of the 4 banger as possible.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000013||terryk||10-01-2001||03:04 PM||||I don't think the light was for CAFE, I think it was for showing off. The shift light was available well past the Fiero in other cars.<P>If you follow it, it does help.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||1
